  "text": "Recipe: Bonda\nCreator: Meera Arun\nCategory: Snack\nIngredients: potatoes, ginger, serrano pepper, red onion, turmeric powder, salt, water, besan (chickpea flour), chili powder, garlic powder\nCooking methods: cook, bake\nInstructions: POTATOES: Cook chopped potatoes with the skin on with grated ginger, serrano pepper, a red onion, turmeric powder, very little water and salt (to taste) in an Instant Pot. Then mash the potatoes really well. Let them cool completely. BESAN BATTER: Make the batter with besan (chickpea flour), turmeric powder, chili powder, garlic powder, salt and some water. Mix well into batter with dosa batter consistency. BAKE: Make balls with mashed potatoes. Dip them in Besan Batter and keep them in a baking tray lined with parchment paper. Bake at 350 F for about an hour. Check in between and flip them over for even browning.\nNotes: A recipe with BEANS (besan | chickpea flour), TUBERS (potato), RAINBOW VEGGIES (red onion, Serrano pepper, ginger), HERBS & SPICES (various)",
